	\qitem{e}{``The cross-species translatability criterion favors molecular, cellular, or subcellular level biomarkers11 and disfavors organism-specific biomarkers such as the PhotoAgeClock, which is based on changes in human eye corners,96 or the FRIGHT clock, which uses measures of frailty in mice.97``}
