	note={
	\qitem{a}{``Mortality and longevity are outcomes that are difficult to apply in randomized controlled trials because they require long-term follow-up and large sample sizes. A study with the sole objective of lifespan extension would take decades and would be very expensive. Therefore, most clinical projects in progress employ composite outcomes monitoring for the development of diseases in addition to death. Recent synopsis by ref. 4 identified studies (in rodents or human) performed on drugs already approved by the FDA which might have geroprotective effects, particularly those potentially improving healthspan and extending lifespan.``}
