	\qitem{b}{``If there were no disagreement as to the phylogeny of mammals-and few suppositions are more contrary to fact! it still would be possible to base on that phylogeny a variety of classifications not literally infinite in number but certainly running into many millions, all different and all valid and natural in the sense of being consistent with phylogeny.``}
	}
}

